<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guilford, Connecticut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guilford is a town on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-island-sound">Long Island Sound</a> in New Haven County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It was founded in 1639 by English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a> led by the minister Henry Whitfield and joined the New Haven Colony in 1643. The Henry Whitfield House, built in 1639, is regarded as the oldest house in Connecticut.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guilford-connecticut.jpg" alt="Guilford, Connecticut" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dmadeo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guilford-square.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
